<p>It was probably my most technically advanced project to date but what made it even more of a milestone was the fact that build an R package <code>eicmethods</code> at the same time thanks, in no small part, to <a href="https://rhian.rbind.io/talks/2026-02-25-rainbowr-pkg/">an amazing guide</a> by Dr Rhian Davies. I kept coming up with ideas for functions we could now use due to the fresh database access, so I would pivot from one R project to another over a few weeks, building both out as I tinkered with features in one or the other.</p>
<p>Sometimes it’s strange for me to look back and think “this is my job” but as I’ve advanced in my R and statistical skills, I’ve begun delivering intro to data visualisation sessions for professional bodies across Scotland.</p>
<p>What’s made it all the easier to adopt those kinds of skills is the wealth of upskilling resources available along with the highly prevalent <a href="https://design.tidyverse.org/">tidy design</a> philosophy which makes all the information much more digestible.</p>


